    ('22702', 0, $$Long ago, in the small village of Kitete, lived a small boy called Kintu.$$),
    ('22702', 1, $$Kintu loved bananas very much, and he used to eat them every day.$$),
    ('22702', 2, $$One day, a monkey came and stole Kintu's bananas. He decided to chase it$$),
    ('22702', 3, $$The monkey ran into the forest, and Kintu followed it$$),
    ('22702', 4, $$The monkey swung up onto a branch, and started singing a song about sharing$$),
    ('22702', 5, $$When Kintu heard the song, he decided to share the bananas with the monkey.$$),
    ('22702', 6, $$The monkey was so happy, and decided to come down from the tree.$$),
    ('22702', 7, $$Kintu shared the bananas with the monkey, and they ate them in the forest.$$),
    ('22702', 8, $$After sharing the bananas, Kintu and the monkey became good friends.$$),
    ('22706', 0, $$Once upon a time, He-Goat became a believer.$$),
    ('22706', 1, $$One day, he woke up very early in the morning, gathered all his luggage and began to move toward the East.$$),
    ('22706', 2, $$"Hello, Goat! " Hyena said.$$),
    ('22706', 3, $$Then, Hyena said, "We have met, so your pilgrimage has been accepted! For it is said, whoever dies on pilgrimage will have all sins forgiven.$$),
    ('22706', 4, $$"I will tell you three truths," answered Goat.$$),
    ('22706', 5, $$At this point, Hyena burst into laughter and began rolling on the ground. She said, "That is a striking truth! "$$),
    ('22706', 6, $$Hyena ran after Goat and soon caught up with him.$$),
    ('22706', 7, $$Goat said, "The second truth is, if I go back to the village and tell them that I met you but you didn't eat me, nobody will believe it. "$$),
    ('22706', 8, $$Again, Hyena began to roll on the ground with laughter. She said, "That is truth! "$$),
    ('22706', 9, $$Very soon, Hyena caught up with Goat again.$$),
    ('22706', 10, $$Goat said, "The third truth is, if you keep joking around like this, it means that you are not really hungry! "$$),
    ('22706', 11, $$Goat continued running towards his village.$$),
    ('22741', 0, $$It was a second term when our school organised a trip. They charged a large sum of money and most of the students could not afford it.$$),
    ('22741', 1, $$When I heard them reading those who paid for the trip, I also got closer and they read like eighteen student. When the nineteenth came, she was absent but I said, "let me go in this one's place when they do not know". Then I entered the bus, sorry the coaster. During that time I was in boarding in primary seven.$$),
    ('22741', 2, $$When we reached the place, it was *Freedom City* and I was so much excited because it was my first time. Our teachers gave each one of us two bottles of soda and delicious cakes. We ate and enjoyed so much. At that time, it was approaching 1:00 pm and we again went into the coaster and traveled to the beach and it was *Aero Beach*and it was also my first time to go to the beach and I was more excited.$$),
    ('22741', 3, $$Surprisingly,I had not carried the swimming costume and I swam while wearing the uniform!$$),
    ('22741', 4, $$As time went by, we reached a power station and the car was stopped. So I got time to go to washrooms, removed my uniform and squeezed it until it was dry. It was approaching 9:00 pm and we entered the coaster again for the journey. Oh I enjoyed and even fell asleep though other pupils were shouting and one could not enjoy her sleep. Nothing to do, I just woke up and started shouting too. We shouted so much that people wondered who we were.$$),
    ('22741', 5, $$At exactly 10:30 pm, we had reached the *Northern Bypass* and almost everyone was tired of shouting. All of us got asleep and that is when the driver got some breathing space. He drove the coaster at a very high speed because we were late. It was very late and I did not know the time at which we reached Kasubi near our school.$$),
    ('22741', 6, $$I found my mother at school waiting for me but she was so much angry. She barked at the driver and teachers who were around, "How can you take the children to the tour up to this time? " She was not happy at all. In my heart I said, "Let me not mind. After all I have enjoyed the day".$$),
    ('22741', 7, $$We went back home and the following day, the conversations in all the classes were about the trip.$$),
    ('22772', 0, $$Once upon a King who, due to his age decided to adopt a son who will be the heir of his throne because he didn't have any son.$$),
    ('22772', 1, $$He then, called all villagers and he chose ten young boys to whom he delivered seeds, asked them to go and plant them and after two weeks the one who will bring the best result will be his adopted son and the heir of his throne.$$),
    ('22772', 2, $$In one family, one child planted his seed, watered them everyday, did all his best but the grains refused to grow up.$$),
    ('22772', 3, $$His friends advised him to go to the market and buy corn that he will present to the king so that he can be chosen.$$),
    ('22772', 4, $$Time and days passed and the ten boys went to the kingdom palace to show their results.$$),
    ('22772', 5, $$The king took the young boy and said: the biggest quality that must have a king is honesty. All your grains were boiled that means they can't grow.$$),
    ('2278', 0, $$Every morning when I woke up I hurried to eat my breakfast.$$),
    ('2278', 1, $$Then I would take my blue blouse and run out of the house to find my friend Muthoni.$$),
    ('2278', 2, $$Once I found Muthoni, we would forget everything else.$$),
    ('2278', 3, $$Muthoni and I would play hide and seek. I hid in big trees, while Muthoni went behind huts.$$),
    ('2278', 4, $$Muthoni and I went to the village well together. We went to fetch firewood together. We went to school together.$$),
    ('2278', 5, $$We promised each other that we would work hard in school and graduate.$$),
    ('2278', 6, $$But one day, Muthoni did not come to school. I stood at the door to our class and waited for her to arrive. But she did not come.$$),
    ('2278', 7, $$When I returned home that day, I told my mother about my friend Muthoni.$$),
    ('2278', 8, $$I continued with school, but I missed Muthoni very much.$$),
    ('2278', 9, $$But every day I went to school, I looked for Muthoni everywhere.$$),
    ('2278', 10, $$Now I am a lady, but I still miss my friend Muthoni.$$),
    ('22870', 0, $$Kakyo is a girl from Bududa in Eastern Uganda.$$),
    ('22870', 1, $$Today at school she made a new friend called Nankya.$$),
    ('22870', 2, $$Nankya is from Masaka in Central Uganda.$$),
    ('22870', 3, $$They realized they both like to play.$$),
    ('22870', 4, $$Both girls also like swimming.$$),
    ('22870', 5, $$Kakyo invited Nankya to her home to play and it became a daily routine.$$),
    ('22870', 6, $$They played together everyday.$$),
    ('22870', 7, $$They swam every weekend.$$),
    ('22870', 8, $$And their friendship lasted until they were older.$$),
    ('22971', 0, $$Sheep lived in the city. She got tired of city life and decided to go to the bush.$$),
    ('22971', 1, $$She greeted Hyena over and over again, "Brother Hyena, how are you? Brother Hyena, how are you? "$$),
    ('22971', 2, $$When Sheep heard this, she started running.$$),
    ('22971', 3, $$Lion said to Hyena, "Can't we even find peace in our dens? You throw dust into our eyes! "$$),
    ('22971', 4, $$Lion said, "You are food to me, too, Hyena. Did I chase you? You came to me. Don't blame me later. "$$),
    ('22971', 5, $$Then Lion said to Sheep, "Why did you come to the bush? "$$),
    ('22971', 6, $$Lion said, "Prepare traditional medicine to prove that you are truly a diviner. " Sheep replied, "My medicine is expensive. "$$),
    ('22971', 7, $$Sheep said, "The medicine is Hyena's ear. "$$),
    ('22971', 8, $$Lion ate Hyena's ear and found it so sweet.$$),
    ('22971', 9, $$Sheep said, "Yes, it is possible my king. " So Lion cut off Hyena's second ear and brought it to Sheep.$$),
    ('22971', 10, $$Then Lion said to Sheep, "Is it possible to get the skin? " Sheep replied, "I think it is possible my king. "$$),
    ('22971', 11, $$"If such is life in the bush, then it is better for me to return home," said Sheep.$$),
